Two fixes:
	1.	On each job card, put the “Last run” status badge and its timestamp on the same line (e.g., “Last run: [success/failed badge] · 8/30/2026, 8:36:55 AM”) instead of the timestamp wrapping to a new line below. This is purely to reduce each card’s vertical height as more jobs get added later.
	2.	Fix the tab-filter animation: switching between two non-“All” tabs directly (e.g., Kubernetes → Database) doesn’t animate at all, while switching to/from “All” does. This is almost certainly because the filtered job cards aren’t keyed by a stable unique identifier. Audit the AnimatePresence-wrapped job list and ensure every card’s key is the job’s unique ID (e.g. job.id), never an array index or any value derived from the current tab. Also confirm the list container itself isn’t keyed in a way that only changes for “All” vs “not All” (e.g. key={activeTab === 'all' ? 'all' : 'filtered'}) — remove any such grouping so AnimatePresence can correctly detect additions/removals/reorders between any two tabs, not just ones involving “All”.
